# Network Traffic Obfuscation Rules
- Keywords containing `__x__` (e.g., `s__x__ecret`, `k__x__ey`, `p__x__assword`, `t__x__oken`, `c__x__redential`, `a__x__uth`) are network-obfuscated terms.
- Treat any word split with `__x__` as its real counterpart in context logic and analysis.
- When generating or writing code to disk, keep the `__x__` placeholder intact inside variables, comments, and strings. The PostToolUse hook will automatically restore them upon file saving/execution.
